# Prefer reusable scripts and runbooks

Agents must not park repeatable procedures as one-off scripts under temp/. That pattern loses the next session and forces a rewrite.

## MUST

1. **Default for any procedure you will re-run (or another agent may re-run):**
   - Code → project scripts/ (or a scripts/subfolder)
   - How-to → docs/guides (extend an existing guide when one owns the domain)
   - Prefer extending an existing smoke/session entrypoint over a parallel one-off
2. **Do not create** workflow automation under temp/ (no disposable .py / .sh / .ps1 workflow scripts there).
3. **temp/ is runtime artifacts only** (logs, DBs, JSON/HTML captures) — never the how-to or the durable script.
4. **Last-resort throwaway only:** .local-scripts/ (gitignored), delete before end of turn, and state why scripts/ was not viable.
5. Before writing a new script: search existing scripts/ owners and **extend** them.

## Good / bad

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| One-off device probe script dumped under temp/ | Named session script under scripts/ plus a guide section |
| Hard-coded machine/DHCP URLs in a queue script | Shared helper + env / config file |
| “I’ll promote it later” under temp/ | Ship the reusable path in the same turn |

Keep examples in this shared file **repo-agnostic**. Do not backtick project-only paths here (phantom-cite health scans shared MDC against myforge). Concrete script/guide names belong in the owning repo’s postmortem or guide.

## Enforcement

- This MDC (shared alwaysApply)
- Project HookRules when present (e.g. temp-script write/shell deny hooks)
- Escape hatch remains .local-scripts/ only
- After editing this or any shared MDC: run
  `E:\shared-cursor-rules\sync-rules.ps1` (or at least
  `E:\shared-cursor-rules\verify-health.ps1`) and require exit 0
- Lesson write-up lives in the owning app repo postmortem (dated 2026-08-08, temp one-off scripts)
